*> PLB-C037 search-index-not-set: a serial SEARCH starts at the current
*> value of the table's first index. The paragraph should set it first.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SEARCHES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  CODE-TABLE.
    05  CODE-ENTRY      PIC X(3) OCCURS 20 TIMES
                        INDEXED BY CODE-IX CODE-IX2.
01  SORTED-TABLE.
    05  SORTED-ENTRY    PIC X(3) OCCURS 20 TIMES
                        ASCENDING KEY IS SORTED-ENTRY
                        INDEXED BY SORTED-IX.
01  WANTED              PIC X(3) VALUE "ABC".
01  FOUND-FLAG          PIC X VALUE "N".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    PERFORM FIND-FIRST
    PERFORM FIND-AGAIN
    PERFORM FIND-SET-ELSEWHERE
    PERFORM FIND-SORTED
    PERFORM FIND-IN-LOOP
    DISPLAY FOUND-FLAG
    STOP RUN.
FIND-FIRST.
    SET CODE-IX TO 1
    SEARCH CODE-ENTRY
        AT END MOVE "N" TO FOUND-FLAG
        WHEN CODE-ENTRY(CODE-IX) = WANTED
            MOVE "Y" TO FOUND-FLAG
    END-SEARCH.
FIND-AGAIN.
    SEARCH CODE-ENTRY
        AT END MOVE "N" TO FOUND-FLAG
        WHEN CODE-ENTRY(CODE-IX) = WANTED
            MOVE "Y" TO FOUND-FLAG
    END-SEARCH.
FIND-SET-ELSEWHERE.
    SET CODE-IX2 TO 1
    SEARCH CODE-ENTRY VARYING CODE-IX2
        WHEN CODE-ENTRY(CODE-IX) = WANTED
            MOVE "Y" TO FOUND-FLAG
    END-SEARCH.
FIND-SORTED.
    SEARCH ALL SORTED-ENTRY
        WHEN SORTED-ENTRY(SORTED-IX) = WANTED
            MOVE "Y" TO FOUND-FLAG
    END-SEARCH.
FIND-IN-LOOP.
    PERFORM VARYING CODE-IX FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CODE-IX > 20
        SEARCH CODE-ENTRY
            WHEN CODE-ENTRY(CODE-IX) = WANTED
                MOVE "Y" TO FOUND-FLAG
        END-SEARCH
    END-PERFORM.
